), better known by his stage name V.I.C., is an American rapper from Atlanta, Georgia. His hit single, \"Get Silly\", reached #29 on the Billboard Hot 100 chart in 2008. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/V.I.C.\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Bruce Banna',382,3194,'Shady Nate',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Bruce+Banna\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('C.O.S.',1142,31612,'Doomsday Productions',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/C.O.S.\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Don Joe',27197,627978,'NIGHT SKINNY',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Don+Joe\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('C.W. Da Youngblood',257,4250,'CW Da Youngblood',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/C.W.+Da+Youngblood\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Soso',28414,373316,'Moka Only','There are at least two bands that use the name \"Soso\":\n\n1. Canadian hiphop artist Troy Gronsdahl\n2. Swedish synthpop artist Sophia Somajo\n3. Polish hiphop group  consisting of Kaczy, Lil Gabin, Lil Doppin, Majlo, Biegan\n4. Pop punk band from Sydney, Australia\n\n1. Troy Gronsdahl heads Clotheshorse Records, a label from Saskatoon, Canada home to artists such as Epic, Thesis Sahib, Recyclone, Nestor Wynrush and Maki. The Canadian artist Soso combines his trademark downtempo beats with his emotional voice to get high quality posthop. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Soso\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Economics',201,3168,'Carbon Dating Service','Economics, aka Dean Summach, has been quietly making compelling instrumental music from his hometown of Saskatoon,  Saskatchewan for the past decade. economics\' songs are an ambitious collection of dense and delicate songs, falling somewhere in between adventurous post-rock, instrumental hip-hop, and vintage electro-pop. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Economics\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Brainpower',64554,810774,'The Opposites','Brainpower (or MC Brainpower) is a Dutch rapper born in Belgium (Gerrit-Jan (Gert-Jan) Mulder - Antwerpen, Belgium 5 februari 1975). His family moved to Alphen aan den Rijn, The Netherlands were he was introduced to hip hop and rap. In the early 90s he moved to Amsterdam, The Netherlands\n\nBrainpower whose career rocketed after winning the Grand Prix of the Dutch Talent Show in 1998. Together with his long time friend and collaborator turntablist DJ TLM (www. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Brainpower\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Brianna Perry',3747,35292,'Nyemiah Supreme','Brianna Perry (born January 11, 1992), also known as Lil\' Brianna, is an American female rapper from Miami-Dade County, Florida. She was the youngest act signed to Missy Elliott\'s label The Goldmind Inc. and affiliated with Slip-N-Slide Records, home to rappers Trina and Rick Ross. Perry made her debut on Trina\'s album Diamond Princess on the track \"Kandi\". Since then, she has released six mixtapes, four mainstream singles and various viral freestyles.\n\n <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Brianna+Perry\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('C.W. Da Youngblood',257,4250,'CW Da Youngblood',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/C.W.+Da+Youngblood\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('C.W. Da Youngblood',257,4250,'CW Da Youngblood',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/C.W.+Da+Youngblood\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('C.W. Da Youngblood',257,4250,'CW Da Youngblood',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/C.W.+Da+Youngblood\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('C.W. Da Youngblood',257,4250,'CW Da Youngblood',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/C.W.+Da+Youngblood\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Mr Phormula',583,4255,'Sŵnami','Mr Phormula is Welsh beat-boxer and rap artist Ed Holden (born in 1984) from  Llanfrothen, Gwynedd.  <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Mr+Phormula\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('The Gumshoe Strut',433,3086,'Pip Skid','Underground rapper from Vancouver, Canada. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/The+Gumshoe+Strut\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Cream',2752495,45991919,'Derek and the Dominos','Cream was a British rock supergroup formed in London in 1966. The group consisted of bassist Jack Bruce, guitarist Eric Clapton, and drummer Ginger Baker. Jack Bruce was the primary songwriter and vocalist, with contributions from Clapton and Baker. The band members had previously been part of successful groups, and Cream is often recognized as one of the first supergroups. The band was known for the instrumental skills of its members.\n\nDuring their career from 1966 to 1968 <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Cream\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Cream',2752495,45991919,'Derek and the Dominos','Cream was a British rock supergroup formed in London in 1966. The group consisted of bassist Jack Bruce, guitarist Eric Clapton, and drummer Ginger Baker. Jack Bruce was the primary songwriter and vocalist, with contributions from Clapton and Baker. The band members had previously been part of successful groups, and Cream is often recognized as one of the first supergroups. The band was known for the instrumental skills of its members.\n\nDuring their career from 1966 to 1968 <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Cream\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('KingKhan',351,2854,'dvnots',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/KingKhan\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Ben Jones',11079,58969,'Jo Russell','Ben Jones was the singer and songwriter for The Lovedays. He has produced The Soundcasters, Scott Brunger and Rich Clark independently, and is a multi instrumentalist. \nHe released his first solo album, \"Echobox\" in 2010, swiftly followed by his second, \"Kaleidoscope\" in 2011.\nBoth were met with critical acclaim. He is currently writing the \"difficult\" third album, and also co-writing an album with Maxine Kerr. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Ben+Jones\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('C-Lance',7509,57916,'Connor Gilbert',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/C-Lance\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Jack Danz',1950,31668,'Cult of the Damned',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Jack+Danz\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('sk!nt',66,1066,'Res One','Reuben Ansfield Pouralli  born December 1988. Also known as the multi-genre producer sk!nt. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/sk%21nt\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Pyoot',21,122,'Joey Stylez',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Pyoot\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('GT',20597,86458,'The Attic Sleepers','1. GT is a rapper from the eastisde of Detroit, MI. He is currently signed to Street Lord Juan\'s record label, Dirty Glove Entertainment. While prepping his solo album, he has released an EP and has worked with some of the biggest and upcoming names in the Detroit rap scene.\n\n2. Gabor Turucz, better known as “GT” has been producing electronic music since ’97 and started DJing in 2000. His preferred genres are progressive-, electro-, tech-house, techno and breaks. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/GT\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Willie the Kid',33254,507680,'Flee Lord','The son of a DJ who was down with the culture from its onset, Willie grew up in a home where Hip-Hop was the ideology of choice, in Grand Rapids, MI. “We never got in trouble for throwing footballs in the house, we got in trouble for scratching records, or playing a rap record and saying the cuss words.” Around the age of 12, as his brother, La the Darkman, got his industry break through a deal with Wu Tang, Willie the Kid got his first notebook and truly started writing. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Willie+the+Kid\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('C.W. Da Youngblood',257,4250,'CW Da Youngblood',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/C.W.+Da+Youngblood\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('GoldenB',91,636,'Danisen',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/GoldenB\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Jonathan Cloud',665,4656,'Denzill Jones',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Jonathan+Cloud\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Agirbest',25,63,'Beytocan',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Agirbest\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Elemental',43300,913261,'Detour','There are multiple artists using the name Elemental:\n1) A Croatian hip-hop band, founded in 1998.\n2) A hip-hop MC from Brighton\n3) A British dubstep producer.\n4) D&B/autonomic producer from Bristol / London, Britain (UK). Signed to Runtime Records.\n5) Psybient/psychill producer from Romania\n6. A groove metal band from Quito, Ecuador.\n7. A black metal band from Finland.\n\n1)\nElemental is a Croatian hip-hop band, founded in 1998. It consisted of three MCs. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Elemental\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Skitz',18629,144714,'Yungun','Skitz is a DJ, producer and recording artist releasing hip hop records. He co-presented the Original Fever show with Rodney P on BBC 1Xtra radio station until 2007. His first full length album, Countryman, was released in 2001. His latest is the 2010 release Sticksman which was accompanied by a remixed version entitled Remicksman. He has also released a number of mix CDs including Badmeaningood and the Homegrown series as well as countless singles. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Skitz\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('BullY BeatZ',92,398,'Dj DIREKT',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/BullY+BeatZ\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Brighty',489,2588,'Chris Bullen',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Brighty\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Infinite Mass',51124,545257,'Thomas Rusiak','Infinite Mass is a Swedish hip hop group formed in 1991 by Rodrigo Pencheff (of  The Latin Kings fame together with  Dogge Doggelito), Amir Chamdin and Bechir Eklund. In 1992 the group won the talent show Swedish Championship of Rap. The same year, they achieved fame when they participated in the movie \"Sökarna\" (The Seekers) and released the single \"Shoot the Racist\" which was later renamed \"Area Turns Red\". There was some controversy in the Swedish mass media at the time regarding the song\'s lyrics. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Infinite+Mass\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Pce Bj',2945,35449,'Lilqua 50',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Pce+Bj\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Tucker HD',45,463,'Byg Ben Sukuya',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Tucker+HD\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Ben Jones',11079,58969,'Jo Russell','Ben Jones was the singer and songwriter for The Lovedays. He has produced The Soundcasters, Scott Brunger and Rich Clark independently, and is a multi instrumentalist. \nHe released his first solo album, \"Echobox\" in 2010, swiftly followed by his second, \"Kaleidoscope\" in 2011.\nBoth were met with critical acclaim. He is currently writing the \"difficult\" third album, and also co-writing an album with Maxine Kerr. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Ben+Jones\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('bigmcenroe',56,560,'Bazooka Joe 204',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/bigmcenroe\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Ban-T',175,501,'Frost Legato',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Ban-T\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Razor Man',253,1563,'Caleb Awiti',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Razor+Man\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Aktion',2512,9541,'The Magnificent Zenians','There is more than one artist using the name Aktion.\n\n1) Claude Maki (真木蔵人, Maki Kurōdo?)  (born October 3, 1972) is a Japanese surfing champion, actor and j-urban artist, under the stage name AKTION, from Akasaka Tokyo . He is the eldest son of actor and singer Mike Maki.\n\nHis size is 173cm and his hobby is surfing. He made his television acting debut in 1987, at age 15, in NHK\'s year-long Japanese period drama series Takeda Shingen. Also that year, he made his motion picture debut in Soul Music Lovers Only. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Aktion\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Sagi Braitner',289,3423,'Eden Hason',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Sagi+Braitner\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Najee Janey',385,1247,'Milkshaw Benedict',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Najee+Janey\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('PLEASEBENiCE',454,2452,'Mushy Krongold',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/PLEASEBENiCE\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Ronald Morrera',230,1719,'Deezy Tha Don',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Ronald+Morrera\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Fabula',14624,440059,'Pih','rock band formed in lima peru. \n\ntheir music can be heard and followed at\n\nhttp://www.purevolume.com/fabularockband\n\nhttp://www.facebook.com/pages/FABULA-PERU/120706474620393\n\nhttp://www.myspace.com/fabularockband <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Fabula\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Davina Joy',777,8220,'Stallyano',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Davina+Joy\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Mystique',26632,117203,'Wild Side','*Not to be confused with British R&B girl group Mis-teeq*\n\n1. A Trance project from Netherlands from Errol Lafleur AKA Deekai, Mark Nieuwenhuijzen AKA MacMark, Rene van Oosterwijk AKA DJ Rene with singles \"Don\'t Stop Me Now\" (sampling Queens song) and \"Fly Away\".\n\n2. A Greek pop / modern laika girl group consisting of three females: Ελένη Φουρέιρα, Αλκμήνη Χατζηγιάννη & Μαρία Μακρή. They released their debut <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Mystique\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('RICHARDO RICH',168,1171,'lavva',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/RICHARDO+RICH\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Y2',7815,71250,'J.Blaze',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Y2\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Eedris Abdulkareem',4262,20476,'Tony Tetuila','Eedris Turayo Abdulkareem Ajenifuja was born in Kano, northern Nigeria, to Yoruba parents from south-western Nigeria.  His mother left the family home in Lagos while heavily pregnant due to her husband taking another wife.\n\nEedris discovered rap music while he was a student at the Army Day Secondary school and has been writing songs ever since.  He came to public attention as part of The Remedies, together with Tony Tetuila and Eddy Montana.  The group broke up acrimoniously, with the members taking up solo careers. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Eedris+Abdulkareem\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('D Knowledge',92,396,'Samantha Jayne','Derrick I. M. Gilbert (a.k.a. D-Knowledge) is a Ph.D. graduate in Sociology from UCLA. His essays have appeared in the National Black Law Journal, Educational Policy, Encyclopedia of African American Education, Tough Love, and a variety of other publications.\n\nHe has appeared in such films as Higher Learning and Panther, as well as on shows like the NAACP Image Awards, the Arsenio Hall Show, and the Apollo Comedy Hour. Derrick has performed his poetry with such artsits as Me’Shell Ndege’Ocello <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/D+Knowledge\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Shauly',64,596,'Michoel Schnitzler',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Shauly\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('C.W. Da Youngblood',257,4250,'CW Da Youngblood',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/C.W.+Da+Youngblood\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('C.W. Da Youngblood',257,4250,'CW Da Youngblood',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/C.W.+Da+Youngblood\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Louie Ray',25679,243958,'Rio Da Yung OG','Orraccious Quainte Tucker-Brown, professionaly known as Louie Ray, is a rapper from Flint, Michigan who has established himself as a respected figure in the city’s rap scene. He and fellow Flint rapper Rio Da Yung OG are half-brothers. His appearance on Lil Yachty’s Michigan Boy Boat album provided a larger platform for him to showcase his musical talent. Louie Ray is also known for frequently collaborating with rapper YN Jay. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Louie+Ray\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('C.W. Da Youngblood',257,4250,'CW Da Youngblood',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/C.W.+Da+Youngblood\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Mervyn Obiero',132,434,'Sabi Wu',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Mervyn+Obiero\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('C.W. Da Youngblood',257,4250,'CW Da Youngblood',' <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/C.W.+Da+Youngblood\">Read more on Last.fm</a>'),('Twan G.',137,1859,'Young Bossi',' <a href=\"htt